{"id": 15637, "stem": "<div class=\"relative w-full min-w-0 max-w-full self-stretch\" id=\"question-text\"><span><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><mark class=\"bg-transparent dark:text-neutral-100\" data-markjs=\"true\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">A</mark> 35-year-old woman, gravida 2 para 1, comes to the office for prenatal evaluation after a positive home pregnancy test.\u00a0 Her last menstrual period was 2 months ago.\u00a0 The pregnancy was unplanned, and she has not been taking prenatal vitamins.\u00a0 She has rheumatoid arthritis controlled with methotrexate.\u00a0 Ultrasonography confirms an intrauterine pregnancy.\u00a0 This patient's fetus is at greatest risk for which of the following congenital defects?\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b</p></span></div>", "options": [{"label": "A", "text": "Abnormal metanephric differentiation"}, {"label": "B", "text": "Diffuse intracranial calcium deposition"}, {"label": "C", "text": "Disrupted branchial arch development"}, {"label": "D", "text": "Failed thyroid development"}, {"label": "E", "text": "Incomplete vertebral formation"}, {"label": "F", "text": "Interrupted neural crest cell migration"}], "correctAnswer": "E", "explanation": "<div class=\"relative w-full min-w-0 max-w-full self-stretch\" id=\"question-explanation\"><span class=\"\"><div id=\"div_T42328\" style=\"overflow-x: auto; font-size: 1rem;\"><div class=\"group/triggerable\" data-is-open=\"false\"><div class=\"group/draggable\" data-is-draggable=\"true\" data-is-dragging=\"false\"><div class=\"group/resizable relative\" data-is-maximized=\"false\" data-is-resizable=\"true\" data-is-resizing=\"false\"><div class=\"relative max-w-full\"><div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"pointer-events-none absolute left-0 top-0 bottom-0 w-8 z-10 transition-opacity duration-200 bg-gradient-to-r from-white dark:from-nbme-primary-dark-800 warm:from-egg-sour-50 to-transparent opacity-0\"></div><div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"pointer-events-none absolute right-0 top-0 bottom-0 w-8 z-10 transition-opacity duration-200 bg-gradient-to-l from-white dark:from-nbme-primary-dark-800 warm:from-egg-sour-50 to-transparent opacity-0\"></div><div class=\"max-w-full overflow-x-auto [&amp;_td]:min-w-[8rem] [&amp;_th]:min-w-[8rem]\"><table class=\"border bg-transparent dark:text-white border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white hover:bg-transparent warm:hover:bg-transparent dark:hover:bg-transparent cursor-default mt-2 mb-3\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><tbody style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" colspan=\"2\" style=\"width: 72%; font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><mark class=\"bg-transparent dark:text-neutral-50\" data-markjs=\"true\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">T</mark>eratogenic medications</strong></p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"width: 28%; font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Drug</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"width: 72%; font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Adverse effects</strong></p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"width: 28%; font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Phenytoin</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"width: 72%; font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Neural tube defects, microcephaly, orofacial clefts, dysmorphic facial features, distal digit/nail hypoplasia</p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"width: 28%; font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Lithium</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"width: 72%; font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Ebstein anomaly, nephrogenic diabetes insipidus, hypothyroidism</p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"width: 28%; font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Valproate</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"width: 72%; font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Neural tube defects</p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"width: 28%; font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Isotretinoin</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"width: 72%; font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Microcephaly, thymic hypoplasia, small ears, hydrocephalus</p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"width: 28%; font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Methotrexate</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"width: 72%; font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Limb &amp; craniofacial abnormalities, neural tube defects, abortion</p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"width: 28%; font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">ACE inhibitors</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"width: 72%; font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Renal dysgenesis, oligohydramnios</p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"width: 28%; font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Warfarin</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"width: 72%; font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Nasal hypoplasia, stippled epiphysis</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">This patient with an unintended pregnancy has been taking <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">methotrexate</strong>, a folate antagonist used to treat rheumatoid arthritis.\u00a0 Methotrexate <a class=\"hint\" data-exhibit-id=\"exhibit-oca8kgl2yx3v27pfmex4bkrd\" href=\"#exhibit-exhibit-oca8kgl2yx3v27pfmex4bkrd\">competitively inhibits</a><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">dihydrofolate reductase</strong>, reducing the availability of tetrahydrofolate needed for purine and thymidylate synthesis.\u00a0 The resulting <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">impairment of DNA synthesis</strong> particularly affects <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">rapidly dividing cells</strong>, including embryonic cells, bone marrow precursors, and gastrointestinal epithelial cells.\u00a0 Patients receiving low-dose methotrexate typically take folic acid supplementation to reduce adverse effects such as oral ulcers and hepatotoxicity.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Methotrexate is generally contraindicated during pregnancy, as exposure during early embryonic/fetal development can cause <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">pregnancy loss and congenital malformations</strong>, including craniofacial, limb, and <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">skeletal abnormalities</strong>.\u00a0 Folate-dependent processes are essential for neural tube closure, which is normally completed by approximately 4 weeks after fertilization (6 weeks' gestation).\u00a0 Impaired folate metabolism can disrupt this process, leading to <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">neural tube defects</strong> such as spina bifida.\u00a0 In open spina bifida, failure of spinal neural tube closure is accompanied by <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">failure</strong> of the overlying <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">posterior vertebral arches to fuse</strong> (ie, incomplete vertebral formation).</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice A)</strong>\u00a0 Abnormal metanephric differentiation can occur with ACE inhibitor exposure during the second or third trimester, resulting in impaired renal tubular development (renal tubular dysgenesis).\u00a0 Reduced fetal urine production leads to oligohydramnios, which can cause pulmonary hypoplasia, limb contractures, and umbilical cord compression.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice B)</strong>\u00a0 Diffuse intracranial calcifications are characteristic of congenital toxoplasmosis, which can also cause hydrocephalus and chorioretinitis.\u00a0 Congenital cytomegalovirus infection classically causes periventricular calcifications.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice C)</strong>\u00a0 Disrupted branchial arch development can occur with fetal exposure to isotretinoin, a vitamin A derivative used to treat severe acne.\u00a0 Abnormal retinoic acid signaling alters embryonic gene expression, including <em style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">HOX</em> genes, and can cause craniofacial, cardiac, and thymic abnormalities.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice D)</strong>\u00a0 Failed thyroid development causes thyroid dysgenesis (eg, agenesis, ectopia) and may lead to congenital hypothyroidism.\u00a0 Maternal radioactive iodine exposure can also cause congenital hypothyroidism via destruction of fetal thyroid tissue.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice F)</strong>\u00a0 Impaired migration of neural crest cells into the developing bowel can cause Hirschsprung disease, characterized by absent ganglion cells in the submucosal and myenteric plexuses of the distal bowel.\u00a0 The affected segment cannot relax normally, causing functional intestinal obstruction and delayed passage of meconium.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Educational objective:</strong>Methotrexate inhibits dihydrofolate reductase, impairing folate-dependent nucleotide synthesis and embryonic cell proliferation, which can cause pregnancy loss and congenital malformations.\u00a0 Disruption of folate-dependent neural tube closure can cause open spina bifida, in which the posterior vertebral arches fail to fuse.\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b</p></span></div>", "educationalObjective": "Methotrexate inhibits dihydrofolate reductase, impairing folate-dependent nucleotide synthesis and embryonic cell proliferation, which can cause pregnancy loss and congenital malformations.  Disruption of folate-dependent neural tube closure can cause open spina bifida, in which the posterior vertebral arches fail to fuse.\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b", "subject": "Embryology", "system": "Nervous Syst